---
// /blog/veg-vs-non-veg/ — AGENTS.md-bound slug (v1 URL stub points here).
//
// Phase 4 rewrite, and the most necessary one on the site. v1's version of
// this post ran a "Non-Veg Pizza Craze" section recommending meat toppings and
// closed with "whether you are team Veg or team Non-Veg, The Oven Vibe has
// something special for everyone" — published by a kitchen that is 100% pure
// veg (PRD §3). That is a misleading claim on the exact query where the
// pure-veg positioning is the strongest thing we have to say. The post now
// answers the same search intent honestly and owns the differentiator.
//
// (v1 bug NOT reproduced, per the Phase 3 report: this page was missing its
// `<script src="script.js">` tag on the live site, so its footer and reveals
// never activated. It uses the shared Layout like its four siblings.)
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import BlogPostLayout from '../../components/BlogPostLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../lib/data';
import { LINKS, abs, blogPostingJsonLd, breadcrumbJsonLd } from '../../lib/seo';

const headline = 'Veg vs Non-Veg Pizza in Sundargarh: Our Honest Take';
const description =
  'The pizza debate every order in Sundargarh runs into, and a straight answer from a kitchen that picked a side: The Oven Vibe is 100% pure veg. Here is why.';
const image = {
  url: abs('/static/images/og/blog_2.jpg'),
  width: 1200,
  height: 630,
  alt: 'Pure veg paneer pizza from The Oven Vibe, Sundargarh',
};
const path = '/blog/veg-vs-non-veg/';
---

<Layout
  title={headline}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  image={image}
  jsonLd={[
    blogPostingJsonLd({
      headline,
      description,
      path,
      image: image.url,
      datePublished: '2024-05-20',
    }),
    breadcrumbJsonLd([
      { name: 'Blog', path: '/blog/' },
      { name: 'Veg vs Non-Veg Pizza', path },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <BlogPostLayout
    line1="VEG VS"
    lineGradient="NON-VEG."
    subtitle="The pizza debate in Sundargarh, and where we stand on it."
  >
    <picture>
      <source type="image/avif" srcset="/static/images/blog_images/blog_2.avif" />
      <source type="image/webp" srcset="/static/images/blog_images/blog_2.webp" />
      <img
        src="/static/images/blog_images/blog_2.webp"
        alt="Pure veg paneer pizza from The Oven Vibe, Sundargarh"
        class="blog-img"
        loading="lazy"
        width="1024"
        height="1024"
      />
    </picture>

    <p class="subtitle" style="font-weight: 600; color: #555; margin-top: -10px">
      Local log kya zyada pasand karte hain?
    </p>

    <p>
      Almost every group order in Sundargarh runs into the same two-minute argument before anyone
      dials a number: veg or non-veg? It is worth answering properly, and worth being straight about
      our own side of it — <strong>The Oven Vibe is a 100% pure veg kitchen</strong>. Not
      veg-friendly, not mostly veg. Pure veg, by choice.
    </p>

    <h3>Why we picked one side</h3>
    <p>
      A kitchen that cooks both has to keep them apart perfectly, every shift, forever — separate
      boards, separate pans, separate hands, separate storage. In a small kitchen running at speed,
      that is a promise most places cannot honestly keep. Rather than ask you to trust a process you
      cannot see, we removed the problem: there is no meat, fish or egg in the building at all.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Nothing shares equipment with non-vegetarian food, because there is none</li>
      <li>Safe to order for families, festivals and anyone who eats strictly vegetarian</li>
      <li>One set of recipes to perfect instead of two, which is why the taste stays consistent</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What people actually order in Sundargarh</h3>
    <p>
      From our own order history, the pattern is clear and not particularly surprising:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Families and group orders</strong> lean veg, because everyone at the table can share it.</li>
      <li><strong>Paneer wins</strong> — it is the single most ordered topping we put on a pizza.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Weekday dinners</strong> skew lighter: fried rice bowls, grilled sandwiches, a regular
        pizza to share.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Weekends</strong> go bigger — combos, platters, more sides per order.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Is a veg pizza actually as good?</h3>
    <p>
      The honest answer is that a pizza lives or dies on its base, its sauce and its cheese, not on
      what sits on top. Get those three right and paneer, mushroom, corn and capsicum have nothing to
      apologise for. That is where our attention goes: dough that crisps properly, a makhni sauce made
      with cashew paste, and mozzarella that actually stretches.
    </p>

    <div class="highlight-box">
      <h3>Where to start</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Paneer Makhni Royale Pizza</strong> — creamy makhni sauce, soft paneer cubes</li>
        <li><strong>Herb Paneer Delight Pizza</strong> — smoky paneer tikka, jalapenos, red paprika</li>
        <li><strong>Mushroom Supreme Pizza</strong> — loaded, for anyone who likes mushroom properly</li>
        <li><strong>Fiesta Pizza Combo</strong> — pizza, peri peri fries and a drink in one box</li>
      </ul>
      <p style="margin-top: 10px; font-weight: 700; color: #ad210a">
        Every pizza is a 7-inch regular, all under ₹300.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h3>The last slice</h3>
    <p>
      If you eat non-veg, we are not going to pretend we can serve you — plenty of places in
      Sundargarh can. What we can promise is that when you order from us, pure veg means exactly what
      it says. See the <a href="/menu/">full menu with prices</a>,
      or check <a href="/sundargarh/">how delivery works across Sundargarh {site.business.address.postal_code}</a>.
    </p>

    <a href={LINKS.whatsapp} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="cta">
      Order on WhatsApp
    </a>
  </BlogPostLayout>
</Layout>
